            "It has long been possible to guard access to your groups, communities and channels using a variety of access gates. This has helped owners and admins to keep their communities focused and high quality.",
            "However, until now an access gate was only considered at the point where a user tries to join a group, community or channel. Of course it is possible that a member's status relative to the required access gates may change over time and so it is possible that we end up with users in our community who no longer qualify. Our new access gate expiry feature helps to address this by allowing an access gate to be re-evaluated for each user on a specified schedule.",
            "You can watch a short explainer video about this feature here or read on below for more details.",
            "**How does it work?**",
            "In all contexts where you can create an access gate, it is now possible to specify a time interval on which that gate will be re-evaluated for all members.",
            "![Setting an access gate expiry interval](/assets/blog/gate_expiry/desktop_set.png)",
            "With that set, users will be able to see that, not only is there an access gate, but the access gate will be regularly re-evaluated.",
            "![Indication that the access gate will be re-evaluated](/assets/blog/gate_expiry/desktop_details.png)",
            "When a user attempts to join a group, community or channel that is protected by an access gate with an expiry, they will be reminded that access gate will be re-evaluated according to the schedule set by the owner.",
            "![Joining a community with an expiring access gate](/assets/blog/gate_expiry/desktop_join.png)",
            "**What happens when a gate is re-evaluated?**",
            "When a you join a group, community or channel with an expiring gate, your membership will be re-evaluated on the specified schedule. Exactly what this means depends on the type of gate. For example, if a channel has a Diamond membership access gate, we will simply check that you still have a Diamond membership. However, some access gates will require user interaction. For example, the channel may require a payment. In this case, another payment would need to be approved by you the user before your membership can be re-established.",
            "In the case where you no longer meet the access gate requirements or user interaction is required to establish whether or not you meet the access gate requirements, you will enter a lapsed membership state. You are still a member in this state, but you will no longer be able to interact until you have established once again that you meet the requirements of the access gate.",
            "![Lapsed membership](/assets/blog/gate_expiry/desktop_lapsed.png)",
            "The process for re-joining is exactly the same as the process for joining.",
            "Note that it is possible that there may be more than one access gate in play since it is possible to have an access gate on both the community and a channel at the same time. These access gates can have different expiry intervals and will be evaluated independently.",
            "**Applications**",
            "There are many possible reasons that you might want to use expiring access gates. The reason that we have a new channel for each monthly airdrop is because we didn't have this capability and we wanted to make sure that someone could not just buy a single month of Diamond membership and then participate indefinitely. We could model this with an expiring access gate now if we choose to instead.",
